     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because 20 mg is double the FDA-labeled maximum for amlodipine, which is 10 mg once daily. Doses above 10 mg raise the risk of peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia. They usually add little extra blood pressure control.\n\nWhich of these do you want?\n\n1. **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily.** This is the maximum standard dose.\n2. **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily.** This is a typical starting dose, and you can titrate up from there.\n3. **Amlodipine 20 mg PO once daily as written.** Please confirm that the dose is intentional. If you'd like, give me a reason to put in the order note, such as a specific off-label indication.\n\nIf the patient's blood pressure isn't controlled at 10 mg, adding a second agent is usually preferred to going higher. That could be an ACE inhibitor, an ARB, or a thiazide-type diuretic.\n\nTell me which option you want and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
